    <statement><p>Let <m>{\bf v}=\vec{PQ}</m>, where <m>P=(-3,-4) , Q=(1,-8)</m>.  Which of the vectors with the following given tails and heads are equivalent to <m>\bf{v}</m>?</p>
<p><alert> (a)</alert> <ul form="popup" name="AnSwEr0001"><li>
<p>Select</p>
</li><li>
<p>Equivalent</p>
</li><li>
<p>Not Equivalent</p>
</li></ul> <m>(0,-2)</m>, <m>(-4,-6)</m></p>
<p><alert> (b)</alert> <ul form="popup" name="AnSwEr0002"><li>
<p>Select</p>
</li><li>
<p>Equivalent</p>
</li><li>
<p>Not Equivalent</p>
</li></ul> <m>(0,0)</m>, <m>(4,-4)</m></p>
<p><alert> (c)</alert> <ul form="popup" name="AnSwEr0003"><li>
<p>Select</p>
</li><li>
<p>Equivalent</p>
</li><li>
<p>Not Equivalent</p>
</li></ul> <m>(5,-3)</m>, <m>(9,-7)</m></p>
<p><alert> (d)</alert> <ul form="popup" name="AnSwEr0004"><li>
<p>Select</p>
</li><li>
<p>Equivalent</p>
</li><li>
<p>Not Equivalent</p>
</li></ul> <m>(2,-2)</m>, <m>(4,-6)</m></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\text{Not Equivalent}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\text{Equivalent}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\text{Equivalent}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\text{Not Equivalent}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><me>{\bf v} = \vec{PQ}=\langle 1 + 3 , -8  + 4\rangle = \left\lt 4,-4\right&gt;</me>
<alert> (a)</alert> <m>\langle -4 - 0 , -6  + 2 \rangle = \left\lt -4,-4\right&gt;</m>


<alert> (b)</alert> <m>\langle 4 - 0 , -4 - 0 \rangle = \left\lt 4,-4\right&gt;</m>


<alert> (c)</alert> <m>\langle 9 - 5 , -7  + 3 \rangle = \left\lt 4,-4\right&gt;</m>


<alert> (d)</alert> <m>\langle 4 - 2 , -6  + 2 \rangle = \left\lt 2,-4\right&gt;</m>


We see that the vectors in (b) and (c) are equivalent to <m>\bf{v}</m>.


</solution>
